# Bind each touchscreen to the output its panel lives on.
#
# The console is a two-output unit: the main UI on HDMI-A-1 (TV / main panel —
# no touch today) and the 7" waveform/readout panel on HDMI-A-2. The 7" is the
# only touchscreen on the current rig, and its controller is a wch.cn
# "USB2IIC_CTP_CONTROL" (USB 1a86:e5e3, verified on the bench unit). Weston has
# to associate a touchscreen with one output; with no hint it picks a default,
# so taps get scaled into the wrong output's coordinate space — which looks
# exactly like the touchscreen being dead rather than like a mapping bug.
#
# The match is per-device (VID/PID on the input device's USB ancestor), not the
# generic ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN class: the final rig adds a second touchscreen
# (the 15.6" main panel) that must NOT inherit the 7"'s HDMI-A-2 binding.
#
# WL_OUTPUT is the udev property weston reads for that association. It names a
# DRM connector, so it must match the [output] name in weston.ini. Change it
# here if a unit is wired with the 7" on the other connector.
#
# The calibration matrix is deliberately NOT here: it is runtime state, lives on
# /data, and is written into 98-segno-touch-calibration.rules by segno-touch-ctl.
#
# See https://github.com/tomassasovsky/segno/issues/659 and
# https://github.com/tomassasovsky/segno/issues/689
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN}=="1", \
  ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="e5e3", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="HDMI-A-2"

# Template for the future 15.6" main-panel touchscreen (controller VID/PID
# unknown until the panel is on the bench) — it binds to the main output:
# ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN}=="1", \
#   ATTRS{idVendor}=="XXXX", ATTRS{idProduct}=="XXXX", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="HDMI-A-1"
